<meta type=article>
  <title | External DSL Sweep>
</meta>

<section | Mermaid diagrams>
In the default (skip) render mode each external-DSL block emits only its contract
markup — a `<pre>` carrying the source verbatim and a `data-enscribe-dsl` hook —
with no rendering library inlined.

<!-- cell: mermaid/form:long -->
<mermaid #fig:flow caption="A simple two-node flowchart.">
graph TD
A[Start] --> B[End]
</mermaid>

<!-- cell: mermaid/form:pipe -->
<mermaid | graph LR; X --> Y>

<section | ABC music notation>
<!-- cell: abc/form:long -->
<abc #fig:tune caption="A four-bar C-major scale.">
X:1
T:Scale
K:C
C D E F | G A B c |
</abc>

<section | Diagram host>
The `<diagram>` host element selects its engine by positional; it renders the
same DSL contract markup as the engine-named tags.

<!-- cell: diagram/alias -->
<diagram mermaid | graph TD; P --> Q>
